A||N||18||Conrad Sanville||Another fiero casualty...||||1||
Z||000000||Conrad Sanville||02-07-2001||10:59 PM||||<BR>I lost my beloved '86GT today due to a snow collapse of my buddy's garage.  I had the car there for winter storage, and i have owned and babied it for a long time. I feel even worse for my friend who lost his Studebaker collection except for the Avanti.  The Fiero is now holding up the 2nd story floor joists along with the roof of the garage which is under a couple feet of snow. He built the garage last Summer. So 10 of the 14 cars that were in there are totaled.<P>I still have my other two Fiero coupes, as they are daily drivers, but will miss GT.  Thanks...||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||02-07-2001||11:01 PM||||I am sorry to hear that!  Man that sucks.  Everyone is having bad luck lately.  Whats up with that?  Well, I hope you get everything worked out and a new GT!<P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">       <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/smiling2.gif">  <BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)  <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/3dlil/eek2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hank is Here||02-07-2001||11:07 PM||||Have hope, Fiero's are tough.  it could still be alive under it all||||reg||1
