Z||000004||Conrad Sanville||02-07-2001||11:13 PM||||Yes, full moon.  And just noticed that this was my 13th post...||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||02-08-2001||10:46 AM||||AAhhh.  That Fiero's tough.  You can rebuild it.  While I was borrowing my buddies truck waiting for my car to get out of the bodyshop, someone ran into HIM! up  in San Jose CA.  I saw not less than six people run red lights and stops signs yesterday while I went to and from work.  Get these guys in a room and teach them a lesson,,,,PHYSICALLY!||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||02-08-2001||10:49 AM||||Man, a brand new garage's roof collapsing?  Now i'm getting worried about my fiero sitting under a 20 year old barn.<P>Of course the body panels are probably shot, but as for the steel, depending on the force of impact, you might not have that much structural damage, maybe just a busted up roof.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Conrad Sanville||02-08-2001||02:37 PM||||<BR>Thanks for the encouragement.  I will go to the site later this afternoon and look at the mess with some daylight. Luckily it is insured and the adjusters will look at it as soon it is extricated.<P>I consider myself fortunate to have found this forum.  Helps alot the hear from other Fiero folk...as I have been driving Fiero's exclusively since the fall of '83.  I will update as soon as I know the status of the GT.  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Bluebottlejunky||02-08-2001||03:34 PM||||I know you could make a chop top?  I think you would be able to rebuild it and make it look better than ever.....Good luck!<P>Mike <BR>Got fiero?||||reg||14
Z||000009||Bluebottlejunky||02-08-2001||03:34 PM||||I know you could make a chop top?  I think you would be able to rebuild it and make it look better than ever.....Good luck!<P>Mike <BR>Got fiero?||||reg||14
Z||000010||Conrad Sanville||02-09-2001||02:28 PM||||<BR>Got access to the GT to further assess the damage. It seems OK from the roof forward, but the building is resting on the rear spoiler and part of the trunk.<BR>The rear suspension is down as far as it can go and the tires appear soft from the weight.  I hope the car holds up until the crew arrives tomorrow AM.  We are now getting heavy rain which will add weight to the building.  I feel much better to have gotten in to see the car and hope it is still salvageable...More later.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||02-09-2001||02:53 PM||||Seems to me that if the rain isn't freezing (or frozen), that it will actually cause some of that snow to melt, and fall off. <BR>Anyway. Good luck.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000012||Conrad Sanville||02-25-2001||09:39 AM||||We got the GT out of the building and it received only slight damage to the spoiler and decklid...Everyone that saw the car when it was pinned under the debris was amazed at how the spoiler and the decklid resumed its shape after the car was removed. It was supporting an amazing amount of weight. I feel so incredibly lucky. Now the poor car has to spend the rest of the winter outside as I don't want to expose it to the salt.  Lets hope for an early spring here in northern VT. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||LZeitgeist||02-25-2001||10:21 AM||||YAY!!!!! It LIVES!!!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Old Lar||02-25-2001||01:08 PM||||I'm glad to hear the Fiero survived the collapsed barn, Did any of the Studebakers survive?  Replacement deck lids and wings are available and or repairable.  Those Fieros are sturdy little cars.  You'll have to bring the car to the FOCONE shows with photos of it in the collapsed barn.||||reg||10
Z||000015||Raydar||02-25-2001||01:21 PM||||Conrad,<BR>Glad to hear there wasn't any more damage. Yes, please tell us how the other cars fared. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000016||Conrad Sanville||02-25-2001||01:40 PM||||Only Studebaker we were able to get out was the '63 Avanti.  It received a smashed windshield and some hood damage. One of the 2X8's went through the windshield and punctured the padded dash.  Only the cars in the front row were the ones we were able to get out including the GT.<BR>The remaining Larks, Golden Hawks and a couple of Supras got it bad since they were located in the center of the building. We had a crew of 12 shoveling off several feet of snow off the remains of the building yesterday. It was one of those corrugated steel buildings 40X50. Squashed down like a tin can. My buddy took a bunch of pictures including one of the GT holding up part of the structure with its tail with the front end up in the air!  I'm using a Dishplayer so I don't know how I can include those shots in these posts...Good thing the Fiero is not a tall car and has those great plastic panels!  Yes i do hope to make it to some shows in N.E. this summer.||||reg||1
Z||000017||TheFiero64||02-25-2001||03:11 PM||||I'm glad to hear the good news.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000018||Tweek||02-25-2001||03:59 PM||||I'm glad that the avanti only received minor amounts of damage. Ive been a fan of them mainly cause I good friend of mine has a 63 or 64.. Cant quite remember... ||||reg||1
